README: NCC Tool - Nina's Circadian Clockwork
================================================

Purpose
-------
The NCC Tool is a command-line workflow for generating reference and target
gene-correlation matrices, computing Clock Correlation Distance (CCD), building
random-gene backgrounds, and testing direct between-group Delta-CCD contrasts.

The tool supports:

    1. Reference correlation generation
    2. Target correlation generation
    3. Randomized background generation
    4. CCD computation
    5. Direct Delta-CCD contrasts
    6. Permutation-based Delta-CCD significance
    7. Bootstrap Delta-CCD confidence intervals
    8. Unmatched or matched random-gene backgrounds
    9. Optional target/background meta-analysis

The reference can be Human or Mouse, provided that the reference species,
reference gene list, manifests, and reference-to-target mapping are configured
consistently.


Basic usage
-----------
Run:

    python NCC_tool.py [arguments]

Show command-line help:

    python NCC_tool.py --help


Required arguments
------------------
    --input_reference_db_file
        Reference manifest/table.

    --l_clock_genes_reference
        Pipe-separated reference gene list.

        Mouse example:
            Bmal1|Clock|Cry1|Cry2|Dbp|Npas2|Nr1d1|Nr1d2|Per1|Per2|Per3|Tef

        Human example:
            ARNTL|CLOCK|CRY1|CRY2|DBP|NPAS2|NR1D1|NR1D2|PER1|PER2|PER3|TEF

    --reference_species
        Reference species, e.g. Mouse or Human.

    --input_target_db_file
        Target manifest/table.

    --reference_target_gene_file
        Tabular one-to-one reference-to-target gene mapping file.

    --target_species
        Target species, e.g. Human.


Reference correlation outputs
-----------------------------
    --reference_full_rho_info
        Detailed reference correlation output.
        Default:
            reference_databases_full_rho_info.tsv

    --reference_weighted_rho_matrix
        Weighted reference correlation matrix.
        Default:
            reference_weighted_rho.csv


Target correlation output
-------------------------
    --target_full_rho_info
        Detailed target correlation output.
        Default:
            target_databases_full_rho_info.csv


Randomization / CCD outputs
---------------------------
    --number_randomizations
        Number of randomizations used for background significance.
        Default:
            1000

    --background_target_full_rho_info
        Background/randomized correlation output.
        Default:
            background_target_full_rho_info.tsv

    --outfile_results
        CCD result output.
        Default:
            CCD_results.tsv


Main workflow switches
----------------------
    --generate_reference_correlations
        Generate the reference correlation matrix.

    --generate_target_correlations
        Generate target correlations.

    --generate_background_target_correlations
        Generate randomized background correlations.

    --compute_CCD
        Compute CCD.

    --compute_delta_CCD
        Compute direct between-group Delta-CCD.

    --run_metanalysis_target
        Run meta-analysis across target datasets and corresponding backgrounds.


Reference correlation example
-----------------------------
Mouse reference:

    python NCC_tool.py \
      --input_reference_db_file manifest.d/reference_mouse_clock.tsv \
      --reference_full_rho_info results.d/reference_mouse_clock_12.full_rho.tsv \
      --reference_weighted_rho_matrix results.d/reference_mouse_clock_12.weighted_rho.csv \
      --l_clock_genes_reference "Bmal1|Clock|Cry1|Cry2|Dbp|Npas2|Nr1d1|Nr1d2|Per1|Per2|Per3|Tef" \
      --reference_species Mouse \
      --input_target_db_file manifest.d/reference_mouse_clock.tsv \
      --target_full_rho_info results.d/_tmp.reference_mouse_clock_12.target.tsv \
      --reference_target_gene_file mouse_human_11orthologue.tsv \
      --target_species Mouse \
      --generate_reference_correlations


Human reference example
-----------------------
    python NCC_tool.py \
      --input_reference_db_file manifest.d/reference_human_adrenal_gland.tsv \
      --reference_full_rho_info results.d/reference_human_adrenal_gland_12.full_rho.tsv \
      --reference_weighted_rho_matrix results.d/reference_human_adrenal_gland_12.weighted_rho.csv \
      --l_clock_genes_reference "ARNTL|CLOCK|CRY1|CRY2|DBP|NPAS2|NR1D1|NR1D2|PER1|PER2|PER3|TEF" \
      --reference_species Human \
      --input_target_db_file manifest.d/reference_human_adrenal_gland.tsv \
      --target_full_rho_info results.d/_tmp.reference_human_adrenal_gland_12.target.tsv \
      --reference_target_gene_file human_human_gene_map.tsv \
      --target_species Human \
      --generate_reference_correlations


Target CCD workflow
-------------------
A standard target CCD run typically performs:

    generate target correlations
    generate randomized background correlations
    compute CCD

Example:

    python NCC_tool.py \
      --input_reference_db_file manifest.d/reference_mouse_clock.tsv \
      --reference_weighted_rho_matrix results.d/reference_mouse_clock_12.weighted_rho.csv \
      --l_clock_genes_reference "Bmal1|Clock|Cry1|Cry2|Dbp|Npas2|Nr1d1|Nr1d2|Per1|Per2|Per3|Tef" \
      --reference_species Mouse \
      --input_target_db_file manifests.d/target_clock_risk_12.tsv \
      --target_full_rho_info results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.target_full_rho.tsv \
      --reference_target_gene_file mouse_human_11orthologue.tsv \
      --target_species Human \
      --number_randomizations 1000 \
      --background_target_full_rho_info results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.background.tsv \
      --outfile_results results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.CCD.tsv \
      --generate_target_correlations \
      --generate_background_target_correlations \
      --compute_CCD \
      --background_matching_mode unmatched


Background matching modes
-------------------------
The tool supports:

    --background_matching_mode unmatched

or:

    --background_matching_mode matched


Unmatched background
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Unmatched mode samples random gene sets without explicitly matching the target
genes on expression or variance.

This provides a broad random-gene null.


Matched background
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Matched mode samples random genes with similar aggregated expression and
variance ranks.

Parameters:

    --matching_mean_caliper
        Initial mean-expression rank tolerance.
        Default: 0.05

    --matching_variance_caliper
        Initial variance-rank tolerance.
        Default: 0.05

    --matching_expand_step
        Caliper expansion step.
        Default: 0.05

    --matching_max_caliper
        Maximum permitted matching caliper before nearest-gene fallback.
        Default: 1.00

    --matching_seed
        Random seed.
        Default: 42

Optional matched-null outputs:

    --matched_gene_summary_outfile
        Per-gene matching summary.

    --matched_sets_outfile
        Sampled matched random-gene sets.


Matched-background example
--------------------------
    python NCC_tool.py \
      --input_reference_db_file manifest.d/reference_mouse_clock.tsv \
      --reference_weighted_rho_matrix results.d/reference_mouse_clock_12.weighted_rho.csv \
      --l_clock_genes_reference "Bmal1|Clock|Cry1|Cry2|Dbp|Npas2|Nr1d1|Nr1d2|Per1|Per2|Per3|Tef" \
      --reference_species Mouse \
      --input_target_db_file manifests.d/target_clock_risk_12.tsv \
      --target_full_rho_info results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.matched.target_full_rho.tsv \
      --reference_target_gene_file mouse_human_11orthologue.tsv \
      --target_species Human \
      --number_randomizations 1000 \
      --background_target_full_rho_info results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.matched.background.tsv \
      --outfile_results results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.matched.CCD.tsv \
      --generate_target_correlations \
      --generate_background_target_correlations \
      --compute_CCD \
      --background_matching_mode matched \
      --matching_mean_caliper 0.05 \
      --matching_variance_caliper 0.05 \
      --matching_expand_step 0.05 \
      --matching_max_caliper 1.0 \
      --matching_seed 42 \
      --matched_gene_summary_outfile results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.matched.gene_summary.tsv \
      --matched_sets_outfile results.d/target_clock_risk_12.reference_mouse_clock.matched.gene_sets.tsv


Direct Delta-CCD
----------------
Direct Delta-CCD compares CCD between two groups:

    Delta-CCD = CCD(Group A) - CCD(Group B)

Thus:

    Delta-CCD > 0
        Group A has larger CCD.

    Delta-CCD < 0
        Group A has smaller CCD.

Arguments:

    --contrast_variable
        Metadata variable defining the contrast.

    --group_a
        First group.

    --group_b
        Second group.

    --delta_n_permutations
        Number of label permutations.
        Default: 5000

    --delta_n_bootstraps
        Number of bootstrap resamples.
        Default: 2000

    --delta_seed
        Random seed.
        Default: 42

    --delta_min_samples_per_group
        Minimum samples required in each group.
        Default: 10

    --delta_outfile_results
        Delta-CCD result table.
        Default:
            delta_CCD_results.tsv

    --delta_outfile_draws
        Optional output for permutation/bootstrap draws.


Delta-CCD example
-----------------
MYCN amplification:

    python NCC_tool.py \
      --input_reference_db_file manifest.d/reference_mouse_clock.tsv \
      --reference_weighted_rho_matrix results.d/reference_mouse_clock_12.weighted_rho.csv \
      --l_clock_genes_reference "Bmal1|Clock|Cry1|Cry2|Dbp|Npas2|Nr1d1|Nr1d2|Per1|Per2|Per3|Tef" \
      --reference_species Mouse \
      --input_target_db_file manifests.d/target_clock_all_12.tsv \
      --reference_target_gene_file mouse_human_11orthologue.tsv \
      --target_species Human \
      --compute_delta_CCD \
      --contrast_variable mycn_status_unified \
      --group_a amplified \
      --group_b not_amplified \
      --delta_n_permutations 5000 \
      --delta_n_bootstraps 2000 \
      --delta_seed 42 \
      --delta_min_samples_per_group 10 \
      --delta_outfile_results results.d/target_clock_all_12.reference_mouse_clock.MYCN.delta.tsv \
      --delta_outfile_draws results.d/target_clock_all_12.reference_mouse_clock.MYCN.delta_draws.tsv


Common clinical contrasts
-------------------------
MYCN amplification:

    --contrast_variable mycn_status_unified
    --group_a amplified
    --group_b not_amplified

Harmonized risk:

    --contrast_variable risk_group_custom
    --group_a high_risk
    --group_b low_risk

INSS stage:

    --contrast_variable inss_stage_5cat
    --group_a st4
    --group_b st1

Sex:

    --contrast_variable sex_unified
    --group_a male
    --group_b female

Outcome:

    --contrast_variable alive_status
    --group_a dead
    --group_b alive

Age at diagnosis:

    --contrast_variable age_group_18m
    --group_a ge18m
    --group_b lt18m


Target meta-analysis
--------------------
Use:

    --run_metanalysis_target

to request meta-analysis across target datasets represented in the input
manifest. The NCC implementation also applies the corresponding meta-analysis
to background datasets.


Reference-agnostic species configuration
----------------------------------------
Mouse reference -> Human target:

    --reference_species Mouse
    --target_species Human

Human reference -> Human target:

    --reference_species Human
    --target_species Human

The reference gene symbols must match the reference species and expression
dataset. The mapping file must be compatible with the reference-target pair.


Recommended naming convention
-----------------------------
Reference outputs:

    <reference_name>_<gene_set>.full_rho.tsv
    <reference_name>_<gene_set>.weighted_rho.csv

Target CCD outputs:

    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.target_full_rho.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.background.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.CCD.tsv

Matched-background outputs:

    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.target_full_rho.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.background.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.CCD.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.gene_summary.tsv
    target_clock_<variable>_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.matched.gene_sets.tsv

Delta-CCD outputs:

    target_clock_all_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.<contrast>.delta.tsv
    target_clock_all_<gene_set>.<reference_name>.<contrast>.delta_draws.tsv


Pseudocode
----------
    parse command-line arguments

    load reference manifest
    load target manifest
    load reference-target gene mapping

    if generate_reference_correlations:
        compute reference correlations
        write full reference correlation table
        write weighted reference matrix

    if generate_target_correlations:
        compute target correlations
        write target correlation table

    if generate_background_target_correlations:

        if matching mode == unmatched:
            sample random gene sets

        if matching mode == matched:
            match candidate genes on expression and variance
            sample matched random gene sets
            optionally save matching diagnostics

        compute background correlations

    if compute_CCD:
        compare target with reference correlation structure
        calculate CCD
        compare observed CCD with background distribution
        write CCD results

    if compute_delta_CCD:
        select contrast variable
        select Group A and Group B
        enforce minimum sample size
        calculate observed Delta-CCD
        permute group labels
        estimate permutation significance
        bootstrap samples
        estimate confidence intervals
        write Delta-CCD results
        optionally write resampling draws

    if run_metanalysis_target:
        combine target results across datasets/cohorts
        combine corresponding background results


Interpretation
--------------
CCD asks:

    How different is the target correlation structure from the reference?

Unmatched background testing asks:

    Is the observed CCD unusual relative to arbitrary random gene sets?

Matched background testing asks:

    Is the observed CCD unusual relative to random genes with similar
    expression and variance characteristics?

Direct Delta-CCD asks:

    Is CCD different between two clinical groups?

These are separate inference layers. Background significance should not be
reported as the p-value for the direct Delta-CCD contrast.


Troubleshooting
---------------

Reference matrix missing
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Check that the weighted reference matrix exists and is non-empty.

Reference genes not found
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Check that --l_clock_genes_reference uses gene symbols appropriate for
--reference_species and that those genes are present in the reference dataset.

Mapping problems
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Check --reference_target_gene_file and confirm that all required genes map to
the target species.

Delta-CCD groups not found
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Check that --contrast_variable exists in the target metadata and that the group
labels exactly match --group_a and --group_b.

Delta-CCD not computed
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Check that --compute_delta_CCD was supplied and that both groups meet
--delta_min_samples_per_group.

Matched-null sampling problems
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Inspect:
    --matching_mean_caliper
    --matching_variance_caliper
    --matching_expand_step
    --matching_max_caliper

Also consider writing:
    --matched_gene_summary_outfile
    --matched_sets_outfile

Reproducibility
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Use fixed:
    --delta_seed
    --matching_seed


Notes
-----
- The default unmatched background uses 1000 randomizations.
- The default Delta-CCD workflow uses 5000 permutations and 2000 bootstraps.
- Direct Delta-CCD and background CCD significance are distinct analyses.
- Reference and target species must be configured consistently with the gene
  mapping file.
